    <DataNode elementId="AT1G71750-MONOMER" textLabel="hypoxanthine-guanine phosphoribosyltransferase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q8L8L7" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="415" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="THE-ARABIDOPSIS-INFORMATION-RESOURCE, dreher">The HGPT enzyme is capable of acting on two different purine substrates, |FRAME: GUANINE guanine| and |FRAME: HYPOXANTHINE hypoxanthine|, with a higher affinity for the former. Similar to related proteins in humans and yeast, this protein does not act on |FRAME: XANTHINE xanthine| &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; |CITS: [17635220]|. In addition to working on two substrates, it can catalyze reactions in both directions, however, analysis of the recombinant enzyme indicates that it prefers to catalyze the addition of phosphate to |FRAME: GUANINE guanine| and |FRAME: HYPOXANTHINE hypoxanthine|, rather than the breakdown of |FRAME: GMP guanosine-5&apos;-phosphate| and |FRAME: IMP inosine-5&apos;-phosphate| |CITS: [17635220]|. HGPT likely plays a role in purine salvage during plant growth and development. Elevated expression of the HGPT gene and elevated expression and activity of the HGPT protein appear to occur in organs and/or in developmental stages associated with growth or high levels of metabolism |CITS: [17635220]|. In particular, HGPT appears to play a role in seed germination because mutant plants that lack HGPT have a reduced germination rate |CITS: [17635220]|. Characterization of a mutant version of HGPT with an altered ATGA-element reveals the potential importance of this region for the formation of the PPi loop |CITS: [17635220]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT1G71750-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT1G71750.2" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q8L8L7" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-17849, RXN-17848" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="2" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT1G71750.2" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT1G71750" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_17635220" />
    </DataNode>
